--provider
runzero
--provider-name
runZero
--store
assets
--store
services
--store
software
--store
vulnerabilities
--store
sites
--store
certificates
--store
findings
--store
tasks
--row-key
services=service_id
--row-key
software=software_id
--row-key
vulnerabilities=vulnerability_id
--row-key
findings=finding_code
--describe
assets=Assets: one row per device the console has scanned or imported, with its addresses, names, OS and hardware fingerprints, and per-asset counters.
--describe
services=Services: one row per network service, with the parent asset denormalised onto it; service_* keys are the service's own and id is the SERVICE id.
--describe
software=Software: one row per software instance found on an asset, with the parent asset denormalised onto it; software_* keys are the instance's own and id is the ASSET id.
--describe
vulnerabilities=Vulnerabilities: one row per vulnerability instance on an asset, with the parent asset denormalised onto it; vulnerability_* keys are the instance's own and id is the ASSET id.
--describe
sites=Sites: one row per site, with its asset, service, software and vulnerability counters and recalculation timestamps.
--describe
certificates=Certificates: one row per TLS certificate seen on a service, with issuer and subject attributes, fingerprints and validity.
--describe
findings=Findings: one row per finding code raised against the organisation; there is no id, finding_code identifies the row.
--describe
tasks=Tasks: one row per scan or import task, with its schedule, timing and result sizes.
